    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1603">

                <pb facs="1012" n="896" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg896"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.93/59.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Guyant to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 289.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Ensenada</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-12-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 29, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the general subject of
                    assistance to Chinese in Mexico by American Consular officers, I have the honor
                    to transmit herewith a list of the Chinese firms in Ensenada showing a close
                    estimate of the present value of stocks of merchandise on hand expressed in
                    Mexican currency.<anchor n="156" xml:id="d1603-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>From this statement it will be noted that the Chinese have merchandise here to
                    the value of about $100,000, American money. This estimate does not include cash
                    on hand.</p>
                <p>The general fear among local merchants that the Governor will soon commence
                    making forced loans of money and supplies for the soldiers has led the Chinese
                    merchants to make a formal request for the protection of this Consulate.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Claude E. Guyant</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
